diff --git a/research/sources/ideas.md b/research/sources/ideas.md
index 71ee49b..f040a41 100644
--- a/research/sources/ideas.md
+++ b/research/sources/ideas.md
@@ -149,3 +149,22 @@ Each entry: what it is, the address, how it could be read, and what was checked.
 - Same pattern likely at other grid operators (not verified today): MISO's MTEP project list, CAISO and ISO-NE
   transmission plan pages answered 200 but no machine-readable project list was located in the time available;
   ERCOT answered 403 and NYISO did not answer. SPP's list is already on file.
+
+## State-agency copies of county parcels in one schema (Arizona Department of Water Resources) - checked 2026-11-25
+
+- Address: https://services.arcgis.com/C34zQ7veRS0V1t04/arcgis/rest/services/Parcels/FeatureServer (layers 0-6 and 9-13:
+  Apache, Cochise, Coconino, Gila, Graham, Greenlee, La Paz, Navajo, Pima, Pinal, Santa Cruz, Yuma). No login.
+- What it is: ADWR collects each county assessor's parcels about twice a year and rewrites them to one schema
+  (APN, OWNER_NAME, SITE_ADDRESS, SITE_CITY, SITE_ZIP, ACRES_US, URL to the county's parcel page). Owner name only, no
+  mailing address. 1,297,907 parcels in all; Pima alone is 445,971.
+- Why it matters: it is the only free source found for Pima, Yuma, Apache, Santa Cruz, La Paz, Graham and Greenlee.
+- Limit: the licence asks that the data not be passed on to others for re-use, so all seven are recorded as held in
+  research/states/AZ.json. The owner would need to ask ADWR (GIS Analyst, IT Division) or each county.
+- How it could be read: the ordinary ArcGIS parcel reader works (point+distance queries answer). A mailing address would
+  have to come from the county page in URL or from skip tracing, which this run does not do.
+- The same pattern is worth searching in other states with no statewide owner layer: water-resources, forestry and
+  emergency-management agencies often hold county parcels for their own maps (Oregon Department of Forestry hosts
+  Coos County taxlots with OWNER1-3 this way; not recorded because it is a forest-classification extract).
+- Not found today: Mohave County (its own server mcgis.mohave.gov timed out) and Yavapai County (only a 113-parcel
+  extract is public, and its licence grants access 'for non-commercial purpose', pointing to A.R.S. 39-121.03 for
+  commercial use).
